## 14. Disposition of prior findings

Re-verification of statements in `02-spec/25-app-spec-audit/01-audit-report.md`:

| Prior Finding / Claim | Prior Assessment | Current Re-verification | Disposition | Reason |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Clarity on Error Handling | "mostly clear but could use more explicit instructions on error handling" | Spec has zero error handling, no HTTP status codes, no `appfault` mapping. | **Open** | No improvements made since initial audit report. |
| Determinism | "requirements lead to a deterministic output" | Requirements are largely non-deterministic (missing payloads, open enums, undefined permissions). | **Reclassified** | Prior finding was an uncritical rubber-stamp; reclassified as a major defect. |
| Modularity | "plugin architecture encourages small, testable files" | Architectural concept is modular, but concrete files are omitted from the spec. | **Partially closed** | High-level split is sound, but repo-relative file paths remain unspecified. |
| Function Maximum Constraint | "15-line function maximum is strict but documented clearly" | Function length cap is well documented in master coding guidelines. | **Closed** | No contradiction with project guidelines. |
| HTTP Response Codes | "clarifications on HTTP response codes for REST endpoints could further improve it" | HTTP response codes remain completely absent. | **Open** | Carried forward into Finding 2. |

